@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About</PageTitle>

<div class="tool-page">
    <div class="tool-page-header">
        <span class="bi bi-info-circle tool-page-header-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="tool-page-header-text">
            <h1 class="tool-page-title">About</h1>
            <p class="tool-page-desc">Information about TM Mapping Tools.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-page-body">

        <section class="about-section">
            <h2>About this app</h2>
            <p>This app provides tools to assist Trackmania mappers.</p>
            <p>It is built using Blazor WebAssembly.</p>
            <p>AI was used in the process of creating this website.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="about-section">
            <h2>Author</h2>
            <p>Achim Bunke (Ach1oto)</p>
            <ul class="about-links">
                <li>My <a href="https://github.com/AchimBunke" target="_blank">GitHub</a></li>
                <li>Website source code: <a href="https://github.com/AchimBunke/TM_MappingTools" target="_blank">GitHub Repo</a></li>
                <li>TM tool library source code: <a href="https://github.com/AchimBunke/TM_CSharpMapping" target="_blank">GitHub Repo</a></li>
                <li>My <a href="https://trackmania.exchange/usershow/131189" target="_blank">TMX</a></li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="about-section">
            <h2>Credits</h2>
            <ul class="about-credits">
                <li><a href="https://github.com/BigBang1112/gbx-net" target="_blank">GBX.NET</a> by BigBang1112 — C# library for parsing Gbx files.</li>
                <li>
                    <a href="https://openplanet.dev/file/112" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Custom Gates</a> 
                    (<a href="https://github.com/schadocalex/gbx-py/blob/a140ca0f51664fc2e935f40a74f859672ed99861/custom_gates.py" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Repo</a>) by <strong>schadocalex</strong>. — Python implementation of the GateVariantCreator.
                </li>
            </ul>
        </section>

    </div>
</div>